For every \(e=(u,c,c')\in\mathcal E_{\mathrm{OVS}}\), every candidate nuisance \(\widetilde\eta=(\widetilde p,\widetilde m)\) with \(\widetilde p_{a,s}\ge\varepsilon/2\) on all OVS-retained cells, and the signal in Definition \(\ref{def:orthogonal-ovs-normal-signal}\),
\[
E_P[S_e^{\mathrm{OVS}}(O;\widetilde\eta)\mid X]-g_e^{\mathrm{OVS}}(X)
=\sum_{(a,s)\in\{(c,1),(c,0),(c',1),(c',0)\}}
\sigma_{e,a,s}\frac{\widetilde p_{a,s}(X)-p_{a,s}(X)}{\widetilde p_{a,s}(X)}
\{\widetilde m_{a,s,u}(X)-m_{a,s,u}(X)\},
\tag{35}
\]
where \((\sigma_{e,c,1},\sigma_{e,c,0},\sigma_{e,c',1},\sigma_{e,c',0})=(1,-1,-1,1)\).  Hence the Gateaux derivative with respect to either nuisance at the truth is zero.  On the published OVS model, \(g_e^{\mathrm{OVS}}(X)=0\) and \(S_e^{\mathrm{OVS}}(O;\eta)=Z_{e,P}^{\mathrm{OVS}}(O)\) almost surely.  Since the number of rows is fixed,
\[
\|E_P[S^{\mathrm{OVS}}(O;\widetilde\eta)\mid X]-g^{\mathrm{OVS}}(X)\|_{P_X,2}
\le C_\varepsilon
\|\widetilde p-p\|_{P_X,4}\|\widetilde m-m\|_{P_X,4}.
\tag{36}
\]

Suppose \(X\) has fixed finite support and every support mass is bounded below.  Use training-cell averages for every OVS-retained propensity, regression, and conditional moment in Definitions \(\ref{def:orthogonal-ovs-normal-signal}\) and \(\ref{def:crossfit-estimator}\).  Under independent fixed-\(T\) sampling, global retained-cell overlap, the global conditional fourth-moment envelope, fixed-fold cross-fitting, \(\tau_n\downarrow0\), and \(n^{-1/2}/\tau_n\to0\), uniformly over the fixed number of folds,
\[
\|\widehat K_{\mathrm{OVS}}^{-\ell}-K_{\mathrm{OVS},P}\|_{P_X,4,\mathrm{op}}
+\|\widehat r_{\mathrm{OVS}}^{-\ell}-r_{\mathrm{OVS},P}\|_{P_X,4}
=O_P(n^{-1/2}).
\tag{37}
\]
At every support point, thresholding consistently recovers \(\operatorname{rank}K_{\mathrm{OVS},P}(x)\), and
\[
\|\widehat\alpha_{\mathrm{OVS}}^{-\ell}
-K_{\mathrm{OVS},P}^\dagger r_{\mathrm{OVS},P}\|_{P_X,4}
=O_P(n^{-1/2}/\tau_n).
\tag{38}
\]
On the rank-recovery event the sharper fixed-law rate is \(O_P(n^{-1/2})\).  In particular, if \(\tau_n=n^{-a}\) with \(0<a<1/4\), the conservative rate in (38) is \(O_P(n^{-1/2+a})\), its square is \(o_P(n^{-1/2})\), and its product with either root-\(n\) cell-average nuisance rate is \(o_P(n^{-1/2})\).
